a\"->\"ium\", \"media\"->\"medium\", \"mice\"->\"mouse\", \"lice\"->\"louse\", \"boxes\"->\"box\", \"xes\"->\"x\", \"ches\"->\"ch\", and it is case-sensitive for irregulars - \"Mice\"->\"Mice\", \"MICE\"->\"MICE\"). classify inherits all of it verbatim; getting classify byte-exact depends entirely on singularize being byte-exact, which is the singularize owner's scope, not mine.","Embedded NUL bytes could not be tested (argv is NUL-terminated), so behavior on strings containing 0x00 is unknown.","Newline (0x0a) inside the argument was not tested because my line-oriented harness could not represent it; all other 254 single byte values were tested."]

